--- /dev/null
+++ b/custom-kernels-inventory.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Custom Kernel Inventory
+
+This file tracks narrow Python-visible custom-kernel contracts that need a
+consumer selector and focused correctness coverage. It was introduced with the
+Laguna shared-elementwise specialization; older general-purpose operators are
+not yet backfilled.
+
+| Python schema | Implementation | Exact contract | Production consumer | Correctness coverage |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `_C::laguna_m8_silu_mul(Tensor(a!) out, Tensor gate, Tensor up) -> ()` | `csrc/activation.cpp` | Separate, contiguous, 16-byte-aligned BF16 XPU tensors `[8, 256]`; non-overlapping output; bitwise `F.silu(gate) * up`, including the `gate=0x40be` midpoint correction | vLLM Laguna shared expert under default-off `VLLM_XPU_LAGUNA_M8_SHARED_ELEMENTWISE` | Exhaustive 65,280 finite BF16 gate values on every visible XPU, adversarial finite `up`, and guard tests in `tests/test_activation.py` |
+| `_C::laguna_m8_scale_add(Tensor(a!) out, Tensor shared, Tensor routed) -> ()` | `csrc/activation.cpp` | Separate, contiguous, 16-byte-aligned BF16 XPU tensors `[8, 3072]`; non-overlapping output; round `routed * 2.5` to BF16 before the BF16 `shared + scaled` round | vLLM Laguna MoE runner under default-off `VLLM_XPU_LAGUNA_M8_SHARED_ELEMENTWISE` | Exhaustive finite BF16 routed/shared pairing and guard tests in `tests/test_activation.py` |
+| `_moe_C::laguna_m8_moe_gather_finalize(Tensor(a!) output, Tensor moe_output, Tensor topk_weights, Tensor shared, int num_local_experts) -> ()` | `csrc/moe/moe_gather.cpp` | Default-unused strict XPU-only BF16 specialization: separate, contiguous, 16-byte-aligned output `[8,3072]`, canonical routed rows `[80,3072]`, shared `[8,3072]`, FP32 weights `[8,10]`, and exactly 64 local experts; output cannot overlap an input. Consumes canonical row `token*10 + slot` in fixed slot order, relying on unchanged zero-filled W2 rows for remote routes, then preserves BF16 routed, BF16 routed×2.5, and final BF16 shared-add boundaries. | Candidate-only Laguna target-verifier M=8 post-W2 consumer under default-off `VLLM_XPU_LAGUNA_M8_GATHER_FINALIZE`; an explicit shared-output argument distinguishes the dedicated call while generic M1–M8 remains incumbent. | CPU/static schema and source-contract coverage in `tests/test_laguna_m8_gather_finalize_static.py`, plus the independent value-level CPU oracle in `tests/test_laguna_m8_gather_finalize_oracle.py`; XPU exactness gate remains required before record use. |
+| `_moe_C::laguna_m8_moe_gather_finalize_diagnostic(Tensor moe_output, Tensor topk_weights, Tensor shared, int num_local_experts) -> (Tensor, Tensor, Tensor)` | `csrc/moe/moe_gather.cpp` | Diagnostic-only strict XPU BF16 companion to the production tail. Allocates and returns canonical routed-BF16, scaled-BF16, and final-BF16 `[8,3072]` tensors after the same literal helper sequence; it accepts only canonical rows `[80,3072]`, FP32 `[8,10]` weights, and 64 local experts. | No production consumer; component exactness gate only. The production schema and production kernel instantiate the helper without the diagnostic stores. | CPU/static source-contract coverage in `tests/test_laguna_m8_gather_finalize_static.py`; XPU diagnostic equality remains an explicitly later, opt-in gate. |
